    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Tunnel vision plagues the medical profession. One can see it in medical research, in clinical practice and in what is probably its saddest consequence, its future, i.e. medical students. One unintended consequence of all the knowledge that we have at our fingertips is that we have lost sight of the bigger picture, the part where all this information must come together to serve one purpose, to benefit the patient. Research is being done for the sake of doing research. Innovation and creativity are considered inferior to knowledge, not its equals.",
